<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Helghastt. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So I was following the concept decently enough till it got to the anomalous part. Okay, so it’s a sleeping pod, yes? When someone gets in, a gas forces them to sleep. And then what? What exactly is SCP-xxxx-1? What exactly is this “non-physical entity right next to SCP-XXXX”?</p>
<p>I think the physical mechanics of the object are sound. I like your inclusion of historical background as a potential discovery log, as with the potential for the scp to be tested in the field by the Foundation. But I’m having trouble actually picturing the object.</p>
<p>Apart from that, my other main concern is that it’s just not very interesting. I’m sorry to be blunt, but it’s basically an incorporeal capsule that can transport people around? There isn’t much intrigue, tension or conflict present in the concept. One way you can try fixing this is adding some element of danger to the scp. So it can transport people around, but use it too often / too long, and there will be detrimental effects, for example.</p>
<p>More work has to be done here to get to greenlight status. If you decide to revise your concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. All the best for now!</p>

