<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there pattsully. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So this is largely confusing. It’s clear you have <em>some</em> idea of the message you want to convey (the Foundation’s folly etc.) but there are portions of your narrative that don’t make a lot of sense. For example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>woman (SCP-XXXX-01) leaves to get supplies for the town, and when returning notices the SCP Foundation has descended on the settlement.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How did the Foundation get involved in the town in the first place? They would usually investigate initial anomalous activity, but there’s mention of that here other than the severe winter?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>She sees the Foundation as the “bad guys”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's no explanation as to why she feels this way.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and eventually makes a deal with SCP-XXXX</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So she makes a deal with the chiminea? What? How? Is the object alive in some way to begin with?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This ties her to SCP-XXXX, and she is now charged with keeping the fire lit and SCP-XXXX-02 at bay.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There’s still no explanation of what SCP-xxxx-02 is and how it’s link to the other instances. Personally, I don’t even think you need it in the current concept.</p>
<p>Like I said, there’s too much that’s left unexplained at the moment. If you decide to revise your concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. All the best for now!</p>

